  "notes": "The unique principal Muzibu Azaala Mpanga royal tomb exterior:complete broad curved thatched shell with naturally hanging near-soil hem,plain small apex cap/finial,a wide low arched entrance cut into the roof with actual recessed depth,closed dark reed/timber backing,closed ceiling/jamb reveals and earthen entry floor. Sparse original reed/timber framing and geometric lower thatch bundles. Independent gate,drum-house,court,royal-family houses and30-hectare estate remain native;no generic substitute model,no navigable interior or graves. Two ordinary exterior pictures:2025 UNESCO confirms reconstructed thatch while an older full-front picture supplies the complete roof/mouth form. Hidden framing,precise straw pattern,current restored fittings,original support rhythm andfinial are medium-fi approximations. Photographs are not redistributed or used as textures. Exact thresholds,interiors/royal graves,numerical LOD errors andphysical-device timings are outside this acceptance. Circular shell versus decagonal native outline is an explicit map approximation.",
